  "description": "Find the maximum width of a binary tree, defined as the maximum width among all levels, where the width is the distance between the leftmost and rightmost non-null nodes.",
  "target": 4,
  "pseudocode": "1. queue.push({node: root, index: 0})\n2. while queue not empty:\n3.   level_size = queue.length\n4.   start = queue[0].index\n5.   for i in range(level_size):\n6.     curr = queue.shift()\n7.     if curr.node.left: queue.push({node: curr.node.left, index: 2 * curr.index})\n8.     if curr.node.right: queue.push({node: curr.node.right, index: 2 * curr.index + 1})\n9.   width = queue[queue.length-1].index - start + 1\n10.  max_width = max(max_width, width)",
